Now I have to boil the potatoes.
I look at my recipe again.
It has some very short instructions.
First it says: "Scrub the small potatoes clean."
I do that with a small brush under cold water.
Then I read the next line.
Afterwards it says: "Place the potatoes in a pot of water."
I get out my large pot from the cupboard.
I put the whole kilo down into the pot.
The pot is almost completely full.
What is the next step?
The recipe says: "Add a large spoonful of coarse salt to the water."
I take out the salt and a spoon.
I pour the salt onto the spoon.
I add the large spoonful down to the potatoes.
Finally it says: "Turn on the stove."
I put the pot on the stove and turn it on.
Now the potatoes just have to boil for twenty minutes.
